  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.6,
      "end": 2.09,
      "text": "A train ticket reads seventy three."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.08,
      "end": 4.92,
      "text": "Turn its two digit cards around and it"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.92,
      "end": 5.67,
      "text": "reads thirty seven."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.3999999999999995,
      "end": 8.290000000000001,
      "text": "The same two digits are still here."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.7,
      "end": 10.67,
      "text": "Why did the value change by thirty six?"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.96,
      "end": 15.16,
      "text": "The seven loses nine groups of itself when it moves from"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.16,
      "end": 16.349999999999998,
      "text": "tens to ones."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.84,
      "end": 18.92,
      "text": "The three gains nine groups of itself on"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.92,
      "end": 19.73,
      "text": "the return trip."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.28,
      "end": 23.27,
      "text": "The net loss is nine times four, which is thirty six."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.6,
      "end": 25.650000000000002,
      "text": "Here is another ticket."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.1,
      "end": 27.41,
      "text": "Its digits add to eleven."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.76,
      "end": 30.03,
      "text": "Its number exceeds its reverse by twenty seven."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.98,
      "end": 33.42,
      "text": "Before trying numbers, what do those clues tell you"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.42,
      "end": 34.39000000000001,
      "text": "about the two digits?"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.33,
      "end": 41.49,
      "text": "Twenty seven is nine times three, so the tens digit"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.49,
      "end": 42.5,
      "text": "is three larger."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.23,
      "end": 45.5,
      "text": "Set those three aside from the total of eleven."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.949999999999996,
      "end": 47.62,
      "text": "The remaining eight splits equally."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.23,
      "end": 50.04,
      "text": "The digits are seven and four."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.23,
      "end": 53.7,
      "text": "Seventy four minus forty seven really is twenty seven."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.97,
      "end": 58.025999999999996,
      "text": "A three digit code exceeds its reverse by three hundred"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.025999999999996,
      "end": 58.54,
      "text": "and ninety six."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.87,
      "end": 62.14,
      "text": "The middle digit is twice the last digit."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.73,
      "end": 64.47999999999999,
      "text": "All three digits add to sixteen."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.37,
      "end": 66.82,
      "text": "Which code opens the lock?"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.62,
      "end": 72.97,
      "text": "The middle digit stays in the tens column."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.36,
      "end": 74.87,
      "text": "Subtracting cancels it."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.30000000000001,
      "end": 77.56000000000002,
      "text": "Each unit of difference between the outside digits"
    },
    {
      "start": 77.56000000000002,
      "end": 79.41,
      "text": "changes the number by ninety nine."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.92000000000002,
